====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{cx|transitive|lang=en}} To [[cook]] (food) on a grill; to [[barbecue]].
#: ''Why don't we get together Saturday and '''grill''' some burgers?''
# {{context|transitive|Australian|NZ|UK|lang=en}} To cook food under the [[element]] of a [[stove]] or only under the top element of an [[oven]] – {{context|US|lang=en}} [[broil]], {{context|cooking|lang=en}} [[salamander]].
# {{context|transitive|colloquial|lang=en}} To [[interrogate]]; to [[question]] [[aggressively]] or [[harshly]].
#: ''The [[police]] '''grilled''' him about his movements at the time of the [[crime]].''
# {{cx|intransitive|informal|lang=en}} To feel very hot; to [[swelter]].
#* {{w|Rudyard Kipling}}
#*: He had '''grilled''' in the heat, sweated in the rains.
# {{cx|transitive|lang=en}} To [[stamp]] or [[mark]] with a grill.

